# States, requests and errors

A lamp may or may not have turned on. A request, a stored setting and a physical result are three different facts. Never write one as if it were another.

## States and requests

<h2 id="wg-031">Separate state from action</h2>

Label what a device last reported separately from what a button will ask it to do.

<%= example('wg-state-action') %>

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| Reading lamp: Turn on | Reading lamp: Off<br>Button: **Turn on reading lamp** |
| The switch shows On (before the device replied) | Turning on… (pending) |

<h2 id="wg-032">Say a request was sent, not that it worked</h2>

Say “Request sent” until the device reports a result. Say what you saw, not what you hope happened.

<%= example('wg-command-progress') %>

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| Door locked. | Request sent. Waiting for the lock to report. |
| Success! | Home Assistant accepted the request. The lock has not reported a new state. |

<h2 id="wg-044">Explain pending and uncertain outcomes</h2>

If no result has come back, say so, say the request may still complete, and warn before a retry that could repeat it.

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| Failed. Try again. | The garage door has not reported a new state. It may still be moving. Check it before you send another request. |

<h2 id="wg-033">Keep unavailable, unknown, stale and offline apart</h2>

Use the state the source gave, with a time. Say “offline” only if you know the connection is lost.

<%= example('wg-availability') %>

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| Hall sensor offline. | Hall sensor unavailable. Home Assistant cannot get its state. |
| Temperature: 0°C | Temperature unknown. No reading has been supplied. |
| Temperature: 19.4°C | 19.4°C at 09:15. No newer reading. |

A door contact sensor may not change for days. Do not call it stale because its last-changed time is old.

<h2 id="wg-034">Explain what the control can and cannot do</h2>

Show only actions that are supported. Say why one is missing, and who can change that.

<%= example('wg-permission') %>

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| Start cycle (greyed out) | Remote control is off. Turn on remote control on the washing machine to start a cycle from here. |
| Something went wrong. | Your account cannot change the alarm. Ask the household owner. |

Do not add Start, Pause or Reset because another appliance has them. Do not tell people to bypass a safety lock.

<h2 id="wg-035">Keep saved, enabled and running apart</h2>

Say whether a change was saved, whether it will start automatically and whether it is running now.

<%= example('wg-automation-status') %>

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| Automation active. | Saved. On. Not running now. |
| Turned off the hall lights automation. | Future starts are off. A run already in progress may finish. |
| Scene applied. | 4 requests sent. 3 lights report On. The hall light has not reported. |

<h2 id="wg-036">Say what Cancel, Stop and Delete do</h2>

Name the thing, and say what will stop, continue or be lost.

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| Are you sure? | Delete the automation “Porch light at sunset”? This cannot be undone. |
| Cancel | Cancel changes. The heating schedule stays as it was. |
| Stop | Stop the script. Requests already sent are not undone. |

Say “you can undo this” only when the system can really undo it.

<h2 id="wg-038">Make empty and missing states clear</h2>

Tell “nothing found” from “nothing exists” from “could not load”. Label every field. A placeholder is not a label.

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| No data | No devices match these filters. |
| No data | No devices have been added yet. |
| No data | Devices could not be loaded. |

## Errors

<h2 id="wg-040">Give a recovery that matches the cause</h2>

Name the confirmed cause. Offer one step that fits it. Do not guess.

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| Failed. Please restart your router. | The schedule was not saved because your sign-in ended. Sign in again. Your changes are still on this page. |
| Error 500. | Home Assistant could not save the schedule. Try again in a minute. |

Promise kept changes only when they are kept.

<h2 id="wg-041">Tell a mistake from a fault</h2>

If the person can fix it, say what to fix. If it is the system’s fault, say so.

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| Invalid input. | Enter a temperature between 5°C and 30°C. |
| Your request could not be processed. | The heating hub did not answer. This is not caused by what you entered. |

<h2 id="wg-042">Choose urgency from evidence</h2>

Use alarm wording only for a real alarm. A reminder is not an emergency.

<%= example('wg-warning-context') %>

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| WARNING: Boiler service overdue! | Service date needs checking. The saved date is 2 November 2025. |
| Danger! | Smoke alarm: smoke detected in the kitchen. Leave the house and call 999. |

### Write a warning

Put a warning before the step it affects. Say the hazard, what happens and what to do. Use “Danger”, “Warning” and “Caution” only for a risk to people. For a loss of data or settings, no signal word is needed: say what will be lost.

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| Be careful with the cover. | Warning: mains electricity. Turn off the socket at the wall before you open the cover. The plug can stay live. |
| Do not unplug the hub. | Do not unplug the hub during the update. The update will fail and the hub may not start. |

A safety step may stress one critical word in bold: “Do **not** open the cover while the plug is in.” Do this for safety steps only.

### Choose a toast, an alert or a repair

- A **toast** is for feedback the person does not need to act on, such as “Light turned on.” It disappears, so never put anything in it that someone must read to fix a problem.
- An **alert** stays on screen until the problem is gone. Use it for a fault the person should know about.
- A **repair** tells the person what is wrong, why it matters, and gives the exact fix as a numbered list.
- Offer **Undo** after an action the person can reverse.

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| (Toast) Hub offline. Select Settings, then Network, then restart the router. | (Alert, stays on screen) Hub offline. Lights cannot be controlled. |
| (Alert) Fix the integration. | (Repair) Hall sensor cannot connect. Heating will use the last schedule.<br>1. Replace the battery.<br>2. Select **Retry**.<br>The sensor should report within a minute. |

<h2 id="wg-043">Stay inside what the system can know</h2>

Do not give safety, medical or legal advice the system cannot support. Point to a qualified source.

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| Your home is safe. | No smoke alarms reported smoke in the last hour. This does not mean the house is safe. |
| The pipe is not frozen. | The pipe sensor reports 2°C. It does not measure ice. |
